    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1049">

                <pb facs="1293" n="1275" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.24/12–646</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Uruguayan Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Blanco</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-12-06">December 6, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to transmit
                    herewith two copies each of Statement LL–9 and supporting schedules<anchor
                        n="15" xml:id="d1049-f1"/> reporting charges made against the Government of
                    Uruguay during the period from March 1, 1946 through May 31, 1946, covering
                    defense material transferred in accordance with the terms of the Lend-Lease
                    Agreements signed on January 13, 1942 by representatives of the Republic of
                    Uruguay and the United States of America.</p>
                <p>It will be noted that the amount of charges for the period under reference is
                    $21,183.64, and that charges through May 31, 1946 for all defense material
                    transferred to the Government of Uruguay aggregate the grand total of
                    $5,169,379.20.</p>
                <p>It is requested that the enclosed statement and supporting schedules be treated
                    by Your Government on a most confidential basis.</p>
                <p>Accept, [etc]</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Spruille Braden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
